CB_PERFCOUNTER0_SELECT1   <GpuF0Reg:0x37008> <GpuF1Reg:0x37008>   32    {
    PERF_SEL2  8:0  ALPHA {"CB_PERF_SEL_NONE  :  Count nothing " = 0x0, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_BUSY  :  Number of busy cycles " = 0x1, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CORE_SCLK_VLD  :  Number of cycles that the core clock is enabled. " = 0x2, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_REG_SCLK0_VLD  :  Number of cycles that the register clock is enabled. (Non-harvestable) " = 0x3, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_REG_SCLK1_VLD  :  Number of cycles that the register clock is enabled. (harvestable) " = 0x4, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_QUAD  :  This is the number of drawn quads .
Use CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_BUSY as denominator to get per clock rates.
Filtering using CB_PERFCOUNTER_FILTER fields has an effect in this mode. " = 0x5, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_PIXEL  :  This is the number of drawn pixels.
Use CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_BUSY as denominator to get per clock rates.
Filtering using CB_PERFCOUNTER_FILTER fields has an effect in this mode. " = 0x6, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_QUAD_FRAGMENT  :  This is the number of drawn quad fragments.
Use CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_BUSY as denominator to get per clock rates.
  Filtering using CB_PERFCOUNTER_FILTER fields has an effect in this mode. " = 0x7, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_TILE  :  This is the number of drawn tiles.
Use CB_PERF_SEL_DRAWN_BUSY as denominator to get per clock rates.
Filtering using CB_PERFCOUNTER_FILTER fields has an effect in this mode.
 This counter is slightly broken in that it actually counts the number of tiles reaching fragop.  Some of these tiles may be empty when there is fast clear or compression. " = 0x8, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_TILE_VALID_READY  :  Number of cycles the DB to CB tile interface is valid and ready.  This is measured after the input fifo. It counts tiles + events. Subtract CB_PERF_SEL_EVENT to get the count of tiles " = 0x9, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_TILE_VALID_READYB  :  Number of cycles the DB to CB tile interface is valid and not ready.  This is measured after the input fifo. " = 0xa, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_TILE_VALIDB_READY  :  Number of cycles the DB to CB tile interface is not valid and ready.  This is measured after the input fifo. " = 0xb, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_TILE_VALIDB_READYB  :  Number of cycles the DB to CB tile interface is not valid and not ready.  This is measured after the input fifo. " = 0xc, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_FC_TILE_VALID_READY  :  Number of cycles the cmask to fmask tile interface is valid and ready. This interface counts tile times enabled render targets plus events. This will be different from CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_TILE_VALID_READY because each tile is replicated by the number of enabled render targets (events are not) " = 0xd, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_FC_TILE_VALID_READYB  :  Number of cycles the cmask to fmask tile interface is valid and not ready " = 0xe, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_FC_TILE_VALIDB_READY  :  Number of cycles the cmask to fmask tile interface is not valid and ready " = 0xf, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_FC_TILE_VALIDB_READYB  :  Number of cycles the cmask to fmask tile interface is not valid and not ready " = 0x10, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_MERGE_TILE_ONLY_VALID_READY  :  Number of cycles the Merge tile interface has a valid tile-only tile and is ready.  Measured at tile input to merge. " = 0x11, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_MERGE_TILE_ONLY_VALID_READYB  :  Number of cycles the Merge tile interface has a valid tile-only tile and is not ready.  Measured at tile input to merge. " = 0x12, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY  :  Number of cycles the DB to CB lquad interface is valid and ready.  This is measured after the input fifo. This is counting lquad which for fast modes are the same as quads but for slow mode are twice the number of quads. To get the number of quads on this interface use: CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY - CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_32_ABGR/2 " = 0x13, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READYB  :  Number of cycles the DB to CB lquad interface is valid and not ready.  This is measured after the input fifo " = 0x14, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALIDB_READY  :  Number of cycles the DB to CB lquad interface is not valid and ready.  This is measured after the input fifo " = 0x15, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALIDB_READYB  :  Number of cycles the DB to CB lquad interface is not valid and not ready.  This is measured after the input fifo " = 0x16, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_NO_TILE  :  Number of cycles that a quad has arrived over the lquad interface but the corresponding tile has not arrived yet. " = 0x17, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_32_R  :  Number of transfers on DB_CB_lquad using EXPORT_32_R            format. Sum of CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_* == CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY " = 0x18, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_32_AR  :  Number of transfers on DB_CB_lquad using EXPORT_32_AR           format. Sum of CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_* == CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY " = 0x19, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_32_GR  :  Number of transfers on DB_CB_lquad using EXPORT_32_GR           format. Sum of CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_* == CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY " = 0x1a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_32_ABGR  :  Number of transfers on DB_CB_lquad using EXPORT_32_ABGR         format. Sum of CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_* == CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY " = 0x1b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_FP16_ABGR  :  Number of transfers on DB_CB_lquad using EXPORT_FP16_ABGR       format. Sum of CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_* == CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY " = 0x1c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_SIGNED16_ABGR  :  Number of transfers on DB_CB_lquad using EXPORT_SIGNED16_ABGR   format. Sum of CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_* == CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY " = 0x1d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_UNSIGNED16_ABGR  :  Number of transfers on DB_CB_lquad using EXPORT_UNSIGNED16_ABGR format. Sum of CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_* == CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY " = 0x1e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_KILLED_BY_EXTRA_PIXEL_EXPORT  :  Number of quads that were killed because they were an extra pixel export from the shader based on CB_TARGET_MASK, CB_SHADER_MASK settings. " = 0x1f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_KILLED_BY_COLOR_INVALID  :  Number of quads that were killed because their render target had CB_COLOR_INFO.FORMAT set to invalid. " = 0x20, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_KILLED_BY_NULL_TARGET_SHADER_MASK  :  Number of quads that were killed because of null (target&shader) mask. " = 0x21, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_KILLED_BY_NULL_SAMPLE_MASK  :  Number of quads that were killed because of a null sample mask. " = 0x22, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_KILLED_BY_DISCARD_PIXEL  :  Number of quads that were killed because they were blending but enabled optimization to discard all the pixels of the quad. This optimization can be disabled by setting DISABLE_BLEND_OPT_DISCARD_PIXEL. " = 0x23, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CLEAR_QUAD_VALID_READY  :  Number of cycles in the fmask logic that the read_latency fifo to the clear interface is valid and ready. This is counting quads + events. The number of quads should match the number of quads on the lquad interface (i.e. CB_PERF_SEL_DB_CB_LQUAD_VALID_READY - CB_PERF_SEL_LQUAD_FORMAT_IS_EXPORT_32_ABGR/2) minus any quads that are dropped and show up in the perf counters CB_PERF_SEL_QUAD_KILLED_BY_* " = 0x24, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CLEAR_QUAD_VALID_READYB  :  Number of cycles in the fmask logic that the read_latency fifo to the clear interface is valid and not ready. " = 0x25, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CLEAR_QUAD_VALIDB_READY  :  Number of cycles in the fmask logic that the read_latency fifo to the clear interface is not valid and ready. " = 0x26, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CLEAR_QUAD_VALIDB_READYB  :  Number of cycles in the fmask logic that the read_latency fifo to the clear interface is not valid and not ready. " = 0x27, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FOP_IN_VALID_READY  :  Number of cycles the fragop unit input interface is valid and ready. This is counting quads + events. The number of quads here should match CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CLEAR_QUAD_VALID_READY plus any quads inserted by the fast_clear_eliminate (fc_clear) block " = 0x28, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FOP_IN_VALID_READYB  :  Number of cycles the fragop unit input interface is valid and not ready " = 0x29, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FOP_IN_VALIDB_READY  :  Number of cycles the fragop unit input interface is not valid and ready " = 0x2a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FOP_IN_VALIDB_READYB  :  Number of cycles the fragop unit input interface is not valid and not ready " = 0x2b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CC_QUADFRAG_VALID_READY  :  Number of cycles the fmask to color cache interface is valid and ready. This is counting quad fragments + events. The number of quads here should match CB_PERF_SEL_FOP_IN_VALID_READY times the number of fragments created for each of these quads by the fragop block " = 0x2c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CC_QUADFRAG_VALID_READYB  :  Number of cycles the fmask to color cache interface is valid and not ready " = 0x2d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CC_QUADFRAG_VALIDB_READY  :  Number of cycles the fmask to color cache interface is not valid and ready " = 0x2e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CC_QUADFRAG_VALIDB_READYB  :  Number of cycles the fmask to color cache interface is not valid and not ready " = 0x2f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALID_READY  :  Number of cycles the color cache input block's serializer interface is valid and ready. This is counting quad fragments + events. The number of quads here should match CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CC_QUADFRAG_VALID_READY times the number of cycles needed to handle these quads due to any HW limitations like 32bit floating point blending, linear or linear_aligned array mode etc " = 0x30, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALID_READYB  :  Number of cycles the color cache input block's serializer two-lookup interface is valid and not ready " = 0x31, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALIDB_READY  :  Number of cycles the color cache input block's serializer two-lookup interface is not valid and ready " = 0x32, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALIDB_READYB  :  Number of cycles the color cache input block's serializer to two-lookup interface is not valid and not ready " = 0x33, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_TB_FRAG_VALID_READY  :  Number of cycles the color cache input block to tag block interface is valid and ready. This is counting quad fragments + events. The number of quads here should match CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALID_READY + CB_PERF_SEL_TWO_PROBE_QUAD_FRAGMENT. " = 0x34, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_TB_FRAG_VALID_READYB  :  Number of cycles the color cache input block to tag block interface is valid and not ready " = 0x35, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_TB_FRAG_VALIDB_READY  :  Number of cycles the color cache input block to tag block interface is not valid and ready " = 0x36, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_TB_FRAG_VALIDB_READYB  :  Number of cycles the color cache input block to tag block interface is not valid and not ready " = 0x37, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_EVENFRAG_VALID_READY  :  Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (evenfrag) is valid and ready. This is counting quad fragments + events. The number of quads in (CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_EVENFRAG_VALID_READY + CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_ODDFRAG_VALID_READY) equals quads in CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALID_READY as the de-serializer collapses the two cache probe quads back into one. The quads are split into two fifos, evenfifo stores the quads with even 32B address. Events go down both paths " = 0x38, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_EVENFRAG_VALID_READYB  :  Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (evenfrag) is valid and not ready " = 0x39, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_EVENFRAG_VALIDB_READY  :  Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (evenfrag) is not valid and ready " = 0x3a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_EVENFRAG_VALIDB_READYB  :  Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (evenfrag) is not valid and not ready " = 0x3b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_ODDFRAG_VALID_READY  :  Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (oddfrag) is valid and ready. This is counting quad fragments + events. The number of quads in (CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_EVENFRAG_VALID_READY + CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_ODDFRAG_VALID_READY) equals quads in CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALID_READY as the de-serializer collapses the two cache probe quads back into one. The quads are split into two fifos, oddfifo stores the quads with odd 32B address. Events go down both paths " = 0x3c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_ODDFRAG_VALID_READYB  :  Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (oddfrag) is valid and not ready " = 0x3d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_ODDFRAG_VALIDB_READY  :  Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (oddfrag) is not valid and ready " = 0x3e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_RB_BC_ODDFRAG_VALIDB_READYB  :  Number of cycles the reorder_buffer to blend_control interface (oddfrag) is not valid and not ready " = 0x3f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_BC_CS_FRAG_VALID  :  Number of cycles the blend_control to cache_storage interface is valid. This is counting quad fragments + events. The number of quads here should match CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_SR_FRAG_VALID_READY " = 0x40, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_HIT  :  Number of tile transactions that hit cmask cache (TAG HIT && SECTOR HIT). It is a hit if you hit the tag and a sector in that tag meaning that sector's data is valid.
Total probe transactions = incoming tile transactions (in compressed AA mode or single sample with fast clear mode) times render targets = CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_HIT+CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS. " = 0x41, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_TAG_MISS  :  Number of tile transactions that have cmask cache tag misses (TAG MISS).  A tag miss is when there isn't a tag that matches the input.  Because of sectoring, a tag hit does not imply that the required data is in the cache (i.e TAG HIT && SECTOR MISS). " = 0x42, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS  :  Number of tile transactions that have cmask cache sector miss (TAG MISS || SECTOR MISS).  A sector miss is when the required sector is not in the cache.  Tag misses are included in this count because a sector cannot be in the cache if there is no tag for it.
 Total transactions that have TAG HIT && SECTOR MISS = CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS - CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_TAG_MISS " = 0x43, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_REEVICTION_STALL  :  Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled because it is trying to evict a line that already has a pending evict. This can happen when a cacheline has been written out to memory and waiting for the write ack gets a hit again, eventually becoming dirty and needing to be re-evicted. Since only one eviction per cacheline can be outstanding, the cache is stalled " = 0x44, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_EVICT_NONZERO_INFLIGHT_STALL  :  Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled because it is trying to evict a line that has a nonzero inflight count.
When a cachelines LRU count reaches the scaled eviction point set by CM_CACHE_EVICT_POINT and it is still inflight then this counter get incremented
This is usually a sign that the cache is unable to withstand the memory read latency. CM_CACHE_EVICT_POINT can be set to a LOWER value to handle the increased read latency " = 0x45, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_REPLACE_PENDING_EVICT_STALL  :  Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled because the line being replaced has a pending evict. This happens when the cacheline chosen for allocation on a miss is still waiting for its write-ack to return from a previous eviction. This is usually a sign that the cache is unable to withstand the memory write latency. CM_CACHE_EVICT_POINT can be set to a HIGHER value to handle the increased write latency " = 0x46, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_INFLIGHT_COUNTER_MAXIMUM_STALL  :  Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled because one of the inflight counters has reached the maximum value. " = 0x47, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_READ_OUTPUT_STALL  :  Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled because the read request output path is stalled. This can happen due to increased memory read request ask-go latency " = 0x48, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_WRITE_OUTPUT_STALL  :  Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled because the write request output path is stalled. This can happen due to increased memory write request ask-go latency " = 0x49, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_ACK_OUTPUT_STALL  :  Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled because the acknowledge output path is stalled. This can happen if the next stage in the pipeline (cmask cache read latency hiding fifo) is full and stalling the cmask cache so the cache cannot output any transactions. " = 0x4a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_STALL  :  Number of cycles the cmask cache is stalled. This is the combined cache stall signal. " = 0x4b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_FLUSH  :  This is the number of cmask cache flushes. " = 0x4c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_TAGS_FLUSHED  :  Number of dirty tags that are flushed (the cmask cache has 32 tags). " = 0x4d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_SECTORS_FLUSHED  :  Number of valid sectors (i.e they have valid data) per dirty tags that are flushed (the cmask cache has 1 sector per tag). The valid sectors may be dirty. The total valid non-dirty sectors in flushed out tags = CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_SECTORS_FLUSHED - CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_DIRTY_SECTORS_FLUSHED " = 0x4e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CM_CACHE_DIRTY_SECTORS_FLUSHED  :  Number of dirty sectors per dirty tags that are flushed (the cmask cache has 1 sector per tag). " = 0x4f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_HIT  :  Number of tile transactions that hit the fmask cache  (TAG HIT && SECTOR HIT). It is a hit if you hit the tag and a sector in that tag meaning that sector's data is valid.
Total probe transactions = incoming tile transactions times render targets = CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_HIT+CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS. " = 0x50, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_TAG_MISS  :  Number of tile transactions that have fmask cache tag misses (TAG MISS).  A tag miss is when there isn't a tag that matches the input.  Because of sectoring, a tag hit does not imply that the required data is in the cache (i.e TAG HIT && SECTOR MISS). " = 0x51, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS  :  Number of tile transactions that have fmask cache sector miss (TAG MISS || SECTOR MISS).  A sector miss is when the required sector is not in the cache.  Tag misses are included in this count because a sector cannot be in the cache if there is no tag for it.
 Total transactions that have TAG HIT && SECTOR MISS = CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS - CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_TAG_MISS. " = 0x52, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_REEVICTION_STALL  :  Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled because it is trying to evict a line that already has a pending evict. This can happen when a cacheline has been written out to memory and waiting for the write ack gets a hit again, eventually becoming dirty and needing to be re-evicted. Since only one eviction per cacheline can be outstanding, the cache is stalled. " = 0x53, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_EVICT_NONZERO_INFLIGHT_STALL  :  Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled because it is trying to evict a line that has a nonzero inflight count.
When a cachelines LRU count reaches the scaled eviction point set by FC_CACHE_EVICT_POINT and it is still inflight then this counter get incremented
This is usually a sign that the cache is unable to withstand the memory read latency. FC_CACHE_EVICT_POINT can be set to a LOWER value to handle the increased read latency. " = 0x54, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_REPLACE_PENDING_EVICT_STALL  :  Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled because the line being replaced has a pending evict. This happens when the cacheline chosen for allocation on a miss is still waiting for its write-ack to return from a previous eviction. This is usually a sign that the cache is unable to withstand the memory write latency. FC_CACHE_EVICT_POINT can be set to a HIGHER value to handle the increased write latency. " = 0x55, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_INFLIGHT_COUNTER_MAXIMUM_STALL  :  Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled because one of the inflight counters has reached the maximum value. " = 0x56, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_READ_OUTPUT_STALL  :  Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled because the read request output path is stalled. This can happen due to increased memory read request ask-go latency " = 0x57, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_WRITE_OUTPUT_STALL  :  Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled because the write request output path is stalled.  This can happen due to increased memory write request ask-go latency " = 0x58, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_ACK_OUTPUT_STALL  :  Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled because the acknowledge output path is stalled. This can happen if the next stage in the pipeline (fmask cache read latency hiding fifo) is full and stalling the fmask cache so the cache cannot output any transactions. " = 0x59, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_STALL  :  Number of cycles the fmask cache is stalled. This is the combined cache stall signal. " = 0x5a, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_FLUSH  :  This is the number of fmask cache flushes. " = 0x5b, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_TAGS_FLUSHED  :  Number of dirty tags that are flushed (the fmask cache has 64 tags). " = 0x5c, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_SECTORS_FLUSHED  :  Number of valid sectors (i.e they have valid data) per dirty tags that are flushed (the fmask cache has 4 sectors per tag). The valid sectors may be dirty. The total valid non-dirty sectors in flushed out tags = CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_SECTORS_FLUSHED - CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_DIRTY_SECTORS_FLUSHED. " = 0x5d, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_FC_CACHE_DIRTY_SECTORS_FLUSHED  :  Number of dirty sectors per dirty tags that are flushed (the fmask cache has 4 sectors per tag). " = 0x5e, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_HIT  :  Number of quad fragment transactions that hit the color cache (TAG HIT && SECTOR HIT). It is a hit if you hit the tag and a sector in that tag meaning that sector's data is valid.
Total probe transactions = quads in CB_PERF_SEL_CC_IB_TB_FRAG_VALID_READY = CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_HIT+CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS " = 0x5f, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_TAG_MISS  :  Number of quad fragment transactions that have color cache tag misses  (TAG MISS).  A tag miss is when there isn't a tag that matches the input.  Because of sectoring, a tag hit does not imply that the required data is in the cache (i.e TAG HIT && SECTOR MISS). " = 0x60, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS  :  Number of quad fragment transactions that have color cache sector miss (TAG MISS || SECTOR MISS).  A sector miss is when the required sector is not in the cache.  Tag misses are included in this count because a sector cannot be in the cache if there is no tag for it.
 Total transactions that have TAG HIT && SECTOR MISS = CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_SECTOR_MISS - CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_TAG_MISS. " = 0x61, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_REEVICTION_STALL  :  Number of cycles the color cache is stalled because it is trying to evict a line that already has a pending evict. This can happen when a cacheline has been written out to memory and waiting for the write ack gets a hit again, eventually becoming dirty and needing to be re-evicted. Since only one eviction per cacheline can be outstanding, the cache is stalled. " = 0x62, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_EVICT_NONZERO_INFLIGHT_STALL  :  Number of cycles the color cache is stalled because it is trying to evict a line that has a nonzero inflight count.
When a cachelines LRU count reaches the scaled eviction point set by CC_CACHE_EVICT_POINT and it is still inflight then this counter get incremented
This is usually a sign that the cache is unable to withstand the memory read latency. CC_CACHE_EVICT_POINT can be set to a LOWER value to handle the increased read latency. " = 0x63, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_REPLACE_PENDING_EVICT_STALL  :  Number of cycles the color cache is stalled because the line being replaced has a pending evict. This happens when the cacheline chosen for allocation on a miss is still waiting for its write-ack to return from a previous eviction. This is usually a sign that the cache is unable to withstand the memory write latency. CC_CACHE_EVICT_POINT can be set to a HIGHER value to handle the increased write latency. " = 0x64, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_INFLIGHT_COUNTER_MAXIMUM_STALL  :  Number of cycles the color cache is stalled because one of the inflight counters has reached the maximum value. " = 0x65, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_READ_OUTPUT_STALL  :  Number of cycles the color cache is stalled because the read request output path is stalled. This can happen due to increased memory read request ask-go latency " = 0x66, 
                            "CB_PERF_SEL_CC_CACHE_WRITE_OUTPUT_STALL  :  Number of cycles the color cache is stalled because the write request output path is stalled. This can happen due to increased memory write request ask-go latency " = 0x67, 
