                            "SQ_S_SETVSKIP:   @code VSKIP = S0.u[S1.u[4:0]]. @text 

 Enables and disables VSKIP mode. When VSKIP is enabled, no VOP*/M*BUF/MIMG/DS/FLAT/EXP instuctions are issued. Note that VSKIPped memory instructions do not manipulate the waitcnt counters; as a result, if you have outstanding memory requests you may want to issue S_WAITCNT 0 prior to enabling VSKIP, otherwise you'll need to be careful not to count VSKIPped instructions in your waitcnt calculations. 

