                            "PERF_UTC_INDEX_DRIVER_STALLING_CLIENT  :  PERF_UTC_INDEX_DRIVER_STALLING_CLIENT      Number of clocks where the index requester has a request ready but is not being accepted by the UTCL1 driver module; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the UTCl1; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_UTC_INDEX_DRIVER counts  " = 0xb5, 
                            "PERF_UTC_INDEX_DRIVER_BUSY  :  PERF_UTC_INDEX_DRIVER_BUSY      Number of clocks where the index-to-UTCL1 request interface has a request ready for the UTCL1 and the UTCL1 is accepting the request; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the UTCl1; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_UTC_INDEX_DRIVER counts  " = 0xb6, 
                            "PERF_UTC_POSITION_DRIVER_WAITING_ON_UTCL1  :  PERF_UTC_POSITION_DRIVER_WAITING_ON_UTCL1      Number of clocks where the position-to-UTCL1 request interface has a request ready for the UTCL1, but the UTCL1 is not accepting the request; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the UTCl1; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_UTC_POSITION_DRIVER counts " = 0xb7, 
                            "PERF_UTC_POSITION_DRIVER_STALLING_CLIENT  :  PERF_UTC_POSITION_DRIVER_STALLING_CLIENT      Number of clocks where the position requester has a request ready but is not being accepted by the UTCL1 driver module; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the UTCl1; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_UTC_POSITION_DRIVER counts  " = 0xb8, 
                            "PERF_UTC_POSITION_DRIVER_BUSY  :  PERF_UTC_POSITION_DRIVER_BUSY      Number of clocks where the position-to-UTCL1 request interface has a request ready for the UTCL1 and the UTCL1 is accepting the request; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the UTCl1; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_UTC_POSITION_DRIVER counts  " = 0xb9, 
                            "PERF_UTC_SIDEBAND_RECEIVER_STALLING_UTCL1  :  PERF_UTC_SIDEBAND_RECEIVER_STALLING_UTCL1      Number of clocks where the UTCL1 is returning a translated address but the sideband receiver module is not accepting it; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the UTCl1; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTC_SIDEBAND counts  " = 0xba, 
                            "PERF_UTC_SIDEBAND_RECEIVER_STALLED_BY_ARBITER  :  PERF_UTC_SIDEBAND_RECEIVER_STALLED_BY_ARBITER      Number of clocks where the UTCL1 sideband receiver module has a translated address available but the request is not being accepted by the TC request arbiter; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the UTCL1 and TC read request logic; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTC_SIDEBAND counts  " = 0xbb, 
                            "PERF_UTC_SIDEBAND_RECEIVER_BUSY  :  PERF_UTC_SIDEBAND_RECEIVER_BUSY      Number of clocks where the UTCL1 sideband receiver module has a translated address ready and the address is being accepted by the TC request arbiter logic; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the UTCl1 and TC read request logic; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTC_SIDEBAND counts  " = 0xbc, 
                            "PERF_UTC_INDEX_RECEIVER_STALLING_UTCL1  :  PERF_UTC_INDEX_RECEIVER_STALLING_UTCL1      Number of clocks where the UTCL1 is returning a translated address but the index receiver module is not accepting it; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the UTCl1; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTC_INDEX counts  " = 0xbd, 
                            "PERF_UTC_INDEX_RECEIVER_STALLED_BY_ARBITER  :  PERF_UTC_INDEX_RECEIVER_STALLED_BY_ARBITER      Number of clocks where the UTCL1 index receiver module has a translated address available but the request is not being accepted by the TC request arbiter; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the UTCL1 and TC read request logic; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTC_INDEX counts  " = 0xbe, 
                            "PERF_UTC_INDEX_RECEIVER_BUSY  :  PERF_UTC_INDEX_RECEIVER_BUSY      Number of clocks where the UTCL1 index receiver module has a translated address ready and the address is being accepted by the TC request arbiter logic; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the UTCl1 and TC read request logic; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTC_INDEX counts  " = 0xbf, 
                            "PERF_UTC_POSITION_RECEIVER_STALLING_UTCL1  :  PERF_UTC_POSITION_RECEIVER_STALLING_UTCL1      Number of clocks where the UTCL1 is returning a translated address but the position receiver module is not accepting it; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the UTCl1; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTC_POSITION counts  " = 0xc0, 
                            "PERF_UTC_POSITION_RECEIVER_STALLED_BY_ARBITER  :  PERF_UTC_POSITION_RECEIVER_STALLED_BY_ARBITER      Number of clocks where the UTCL1 position receiver module has a translated address available but the request is not being accepted by the TC request arbiter; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the UTCL1 and TC read request logic; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTC_POSITION counts  " = 0xc1, 
                            "PERF_UTC_POSITION_RECEIVER_BUSY  :  PERF_UTC_POSITION_RECEIVER_BUSY      Number of clocks where the UTCL1 position receiver module has a translated address ready and the address is being accepted by the TC request arbiter logic; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the UTCl1 and TC read request logic; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTC_POSITION counts  " = 0xc2, 
                            "PERF_TC_ARBITER_WAITING_FOR_TC_INTERFACE  :  PERF_TC_ARBITER_WAITING_FOR_TC_INTERFACE      Number of clocks where the TC request arbiter has a request ready for the TC request interface logic but the interface logic is not accepting the request; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to TC read requests; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTC and PERF_TC counts  " = 0xc3, 
                            "PERF_TCIF_STALLING_CLIENT_NO_CREDITS  :  PERF_TCIF_STALLING_CLIENT_NO_CREDITS      Number of clocks where the TC interface logic is stalling a client that has a request because there are no tokens remaining for that client; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to TC read requests; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTC and PERF_TC counts  " = 0xc4, 
                            "PERF_TCIF_BUSY  :  PERF_TCIF_BUSY      Number of clocks where the TC read request arbiter has a request ready and the TC interface logic is accepting the request ; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to TC read requests; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTC and PERF_TC counts  " = 0xc5, 
                            "PERF_TCIF_SIDEBAND_RDREQ  :  PERF_TCIF_SIDEBAND_RDREQ      Number of clocks where the sideband requester is making a read request to the TC; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the TC; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_TCIF_***_RDREQ counts  " = 0xc6, 
                            "PERF_TCIF_INDEX_RDREQ  :  PERF_TCIF_INDEX_RDREQ      Number of clocks where the index requester is making a read request to the TC; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the TC; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_TCIF_***_RDREQ counts  " = 0xc7, 
                            "PERF_TCIF_POSITION_RDREQ  :  PERF_TCIF_POSITION_RDREQ      Number of clocks where the position requester is making a read request to the TC; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to the TC; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_TCIF_***_RDREQ counts  " = 0xc8, 
                            "PERF_SIDEBAND_WAITING_ON_UTCL1  :  PERF_SIDEBAND_WAITING_ON_UTCL1      Number of clocks where the sideband request machine has a request ready but the request is not being accepted; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to UTCL1; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND counts  " = 0xc9, 
                            "PERF_SIDEBAND_WAITING_ON_FULL_SIDEBAND_MEMORY  :  PERF_SIDEBAND_WAITING_ON_FULL_SIDEBAND_MEMORY      Number of clocks where the sideband receive machine has a control sideband dword ready to be written to sideband memory, but the memory will not accept the dword because the memory is full; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the control sideband path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_SIDEBAND_WRITING_TO_SIDEBAND_MEMORY count  " = 0xca, 
                            "PERF_WRITING_TO_SIDEBAND_MEMORY  :  PERF_WRITING_TO_SIDEBAND_MEMORY      Number of clocks where the sideband machine receive logic is busy writing control sideband dwords to the sideband memory for use by the index and position machines; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure NGG-related bottlenecks; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other NGG-related perf counts  " = 0xcb, 
                            "PERF_SIDEBAND_EXPECTING_1_POSSIBLE_VALID_DWORD  :  PERF_SIDEBAND_EXPECTING_1_POSSIBLE_VALID_DWORD      Number of clocks where the control sideband requester has made a request for a cacheline, and expects at most only one dword to potentially be valid in the cacheline that will be returned; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the sideband path, as well as finding optimial values for the PA_SIDEBAND_REQUEST_DELAYS register.  A high count may indicate that PA_SIDEBAND_REQUEST_DELAYS values could be increased to improve performance; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND_EXPECTING counts  " = 0xcc, 
                            "PERF_SIDEBAND_EXPECTING_2_TO_15_POSSIBLE_VALID_DWORD  :  PERF_SIDEBAND_EXPECTING_2_TO_15_POSSIBLE_VALID_DWORD      Number of clocks where the control sideband requester has made a request for a cacheline, and expects at least 2 and not more than 15 dwords to potentially be valid in the cacheline that will be returned; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the sideband path, as well as finding optimial values for the PA_SIDEBAND_REQUEST_DELAYS register; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND_EXPECTING counts  " = 0xcd, 
                            "PERF_SIDEBAND_EXPECTING_16_POSSIBLE_VALID_DWORD  :  PERF_SIDEBAND_EXPECTING_16_POSSIBLE_VALID_DWORD      Number of clocks where the control sideband requester has made a request for a cacheline, and expects all 16 dwords of the received cacheline to potentially be valid; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the sideband path, as well as finding optimial values for the PA_SIDEBAND_REQUEST_DELAYS register.  A high count may indicate that PA_SIDEBAND_REQUEST_DELAYS values should be decreased; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND_EXPECTING counts  " = 0xce, 
                            "PERF_SIDEBAND_WAITING_ON_RETURNED_DATA  :  PERF_SIDEBAND_WAITING_ON_RETURNED_DATA      Number of clocks where the sideband request machine has made a TC read request and is waiting for a cacheline to be returned; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the control sideband path, as well as TC latency; all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN counts  " = 0xcf, 
                            "PERF_SIDEBAND_POP_BIT_FIFO_FULL  :  PERF_SIDEBAND_POP_BIT_FIFO_FULL      Number of clocks where the sideband pop bit fifo is full; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks between the WD and the control sideband path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND counts  " = 0xd0, 
                            "PERF_SIDEBAND_FIFO_VMID_FIFO_FULL  :  PERF_SIDEBAND_FIFO_VMID_FIFO_FULL      Number of clocks where the sideband vmid fifo is full; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks between the WD and the control sideband path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND counts  " = 0xd1, 
                            "PERF_SIDEBAND_INVALID_REFETCH  :  PERF_SIDEBAND_INVALID_REFETCH      Number of times where the sideband machine must re-fetch a previously fetched cachline while it polls for a valid control sideband dword; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks between the WD and the control sideband path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND counts  " = 0xd2, 
                            "PERF_SIDEBAND_QUALIFIED_BUSY  :  PERF_SIDEBAND_QUALIFIED_BUSY      Number of time between when the sideband machine writes a PERFCOUNTER_START event and a PERFCOUNTE_STOP event that the receive side of the sideband machine writes one control sideband dword to the sideband memory; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks between the sideband and index paths; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND counts  " = 0xd3, 
                            "PERF_SIDEBAND_QUALIFIED_STARVED  :  PERF_SIDEBAND_QUALIFIED_STARVED      Number of clocks between when the sideband machine writes a PERFCOUNTER_START event and a PERFCOUNTE_STOP event that the receive side of the sideband machine is NOT writing a control sideband dword to the sideband memory.  Counting starts only after the first sideband memory write following the PERFCOUNTER_START event; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks between the sideband and index paths; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND counts  " = 0xd4, 
                            "PERF_SIDEBAND_0_VALID_DWORDS_RECEIVED_  :  PERF_SIDEBAND_0_VALID_DWORDS_RECEIVED_      Number of times when the sideband machine recieved a cacheline that contained no valid control sideband dwords; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks between the sideband and index paths; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND_***_VALID_DWORDS_RECEIVED counts  " = 0xd5, 
                            "PERF_SIDEBAND_1_TO_7_VALID_DWORDS_RECEIVED_  :  PERF_SIDEBAND_1_TO_7_VALID_DWORDS_RECEIVED_      Number of times when the sideband machine recieved a cacheline that contained between 1 and 7 (inclusive) valid control sideband dwords; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks between the sideband and index paths; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND_***_VALID_DWORDS_RECEIVED counts  " = 0xd6, 
                            "PERF_SIDEBAND_8_TO_15_VALID_DWORDS_RECEIVED_  :  PERF_SIDEBAND_8_TO_15_VALID_DWORDS_RECEIVED_      Number of times when the sideband machine recieved a cacheline that contained between 8 and 15 (inclusive) valid control sideband dwords; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks between the sideband and index paths; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND_***_VALID_DWORDS_RECEIVED counts  " = 0xd7, 
                            "PERF_SIDEBAND_16_VALID_DWORDS_RECEIVED_  :  PERF_SIDEBAND_16_VALID_DWORDS_RECEIVED_      Number of times when the sideband machine recieved a cacheline that contained 16 valid control sideband dwords; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks between the sideband and index paths; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND_***_VALID_DWORDS_RECEIVED counts  " = 0xd8, 
                            "PERF_INDEX_REQUEST_WAITING_ON_TOKENS  :  PERF_INDEX_REQUEST_WAITING_ON_TOKENS      Number of clocks where the index request machine has a control sideband available, but is unable to make a read request to the index ring buffer because it has no remaining tokens, meaning there is no room in the TC receive index buffer; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the index path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_INDEX counts  " = 0xd9, 
                            "PERF_INDEX_REQUEST_WAITING_ON_FULL_RECEIVE_FIFO  :  PERF_INDEX_REQUEST_WAITING_ON_FULL_RECEIVE_FIFO      Number of clocks where the index request machine has a control sideband and request tokens available, but is unable to make a read request to the index ring buffer because the index request/receive interface fifo is full; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the index path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_INDEX counts  " = 0xda, 
                            "PERF_INDEX_REQUEST_QUALIFIED_BUSY  :  PERF_INDEX_REQUEST_QUALIFIED_BUSY      Number of times between when the index machine reads a PERFCOUNTER_START event and a PERFCOUNTE_STOP event from sideband memory that the request side of the index machine reads a sideband dword from sideband memory; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks between the sideband and index paths; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND counts  " = 0xdb, 
                            "PERF_INDEX_REQUEST_QUALIFIED_STARVED  :  PERF_INDEX_REQUEST_QUALIFIED_STARVED      Number of clocks between when the index request machine reading a PERFCOUNTER_START event and a PERFCOUNTE_STOP event from sideband memory that the request side of the index machine is starved for work because there is no sideband available from the sideband memory.  Counting starts only after the first sideband dword is read from sideband memory following the read of the PERFCOUNTER_START event; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks between the sideband and index paths; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND counts  " = 0xdc, 
                            "PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_WAITING_ON_RETURNED_CACHELINE  :  PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_WAITING_ON_RETURNED_CACHELINE      Number of clocks where the index receive machine has been told that it will be receiving a cacheline, and is waiting for the cacheline to be returned; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks and performance in the index path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_INDEX counts and PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN counts  " = 0xdd, 
                            "PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_WAITING_ON_PRIM_INDICES_FIFO  :  PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_WAITING_ON_PRIM_INDICES_FIFO      Number of clocks where the index receive machine has a prim dword available from a returned cacheline, but is being stalled by the prim indices fifo being full; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks and performance in the index path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_INDEX counts  " = 0xde, 
                            "PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_PRIM_INDICES_FIFO_WRITE  :  PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_PRIM_INDICES_FIFO_WRITE      Number of clocks where the index machine receive logic is busy writing valid prim dwords to the prim indices fifo for use by the position request machine; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure NGG-related bottlenecks; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other NGG-related perf counts  " = 0xdf, 
                            "PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_QUALIFIED_BUSY  :  PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_QUALIFIED_BUSY      Number of times between when the receive side of the index machine writes a PERFCOUNTER_START event and a PERFCOUNTE_STOP event to the prim indices fifo that the receive side of the index machine writes a prim dword to the prim indices fifo; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks between the index and position paths; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND counts  " = 0xe0, 
                            "PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_QUALIFIED_STARVED  :  PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_QUALIFIED_STARVED      Number of clocks between when the receive side of the index machine writes a PERFCOUNTER_START event and a PERFCOUNTE_STOP event to the prim indices fifo that the receive side of the index machine is not writing a prim dword to the prim indices fifo because there is no valid cacheline available.  Counting starts only after the first write to the prim indices fifo following the PERFCOUNTER_START write; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks between the index and position paths; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_SIDEBAND counts  " = 0xe1, 
                            "PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_0_VALID_DWORDS_THIS_CACHELINE  :  PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_0_VALID_DWORDS_THIS_CACHELINE      Number of times the index receive machine received a cacheline that contains no valid prims; range-1/clk; it can be used to get an idea of the number of valid prims that are being routed to this PA; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other INDEX_REQUEST_***_VALID_DWORDS_THIS_CACHELINE counts  " = 0xe2, 
                            "PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_1_TO_7_VALID_DWORDS_THIS_CACHELINE  :  PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_1_TO_7_VALID_DWORDS_THIS_CACHELINE      Number of times the index receive machine received a cacheline that contains between 1 and 7 (inclusive) valid prims; range-1/clk; it can be used to get an idea of the number of valid prims that are being routed to this PA; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other INDEX_REQUEST_***_VALID_DWORDS_THIS_CACHELINE counts  " = 0xe3, 
                            "PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_8_TO_15_VALID_DWORDS_THIS_CACHELINE  :  PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_8_TO_15_VALID_DWORDS_THIS_CACHELINE      Number of times the index receive machine received a cacheline that contains between 8 and 15 (inclusive) valid prims; range-1/clk; it can be used to get an idea of the number of valid prims that are being routed to this PA; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other INDEX_REQUEST_***_VALID_DWORDS_THIS_CACHELINE counts  " = 0xe4, 
                            "PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_16_VALID_DWORDS_THIS_CACHELINE  :  PERF_INDEX_RECEIVE_16_VALID_DWORDS_THIS_CACHELINE      Number of times the index receive machine received a cacheline that contains 16 valid prims; range-1/clk; it can be used to get an idea of the number of valid prims that are being routed to this PA; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other INDEX_REQUEST_***_VALID_DWORDS_THIS_CACHELINE counts  " = 0xe5, 
                            "PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_FULL_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO  :  PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_FULL_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO      Number of clocks where the position request machine has a valid sideband but is being prevented from making a read request to the position buffer because the fetch_to_primic_p fifo is full; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the position path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY counts  " = 0xe6, 
                            "PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_FULL_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_S_FIFO  :  PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_FULL_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_S_FIFO      Number of clocks where the position request machine has a valid sideband but is being prevented from making a read request to the position buffer because the fetch_to_primic_s fifo is full; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the position path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY counts  " = 0xe7, 
                            "PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_FULL_POSREQ_TO_POSRTN_V_FIFO  :  PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_FULL_POSREQ_TO_POSRTN_V_FIFO      Number of clocks where the position request machine has a valid sideband but is being prevented from making a read request to the position buffer because the posreq_to_posrtn_v_fifo is full; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the position path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY counts  " = 0xe8, 
                            "PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_FULL_POSREQ_TO_POSRTN_S_FIFO  :  PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_FULL_POSREQ_TO_POSRTN_S_FIFO      Number of clocks where the position request machine has a valid sideband but is being prevented from making a read request to the position buffer because the posreq_to_posrtn_s_fifo is full; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the position path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY counts  " = 0xe9, 
                            "PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_FULL_PA_TO_WD_DEALLOC_INDEX_FIFO  :  PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_FULL_PA_TO_WD_DEALLOC_INDEX_FIFO      Number of clocks where the position request machine has a valid sideband but is being prevented from making a read request to the position buffer because the pa_to_wd_dealloc_index_fifo is full; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the position path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY counts  " = 0xea, 
                            "PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_NO_TOKENS  :  PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_NO_TOKENS      Number of clocks where the position request machine has a valid sideband but is being prevented from making a read request to the position buffer because it has no tokens, meaning there is no room in the TC receive position buffer; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the position path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY and PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN counts  " = 0xeb, 
                            "PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_NO_PRIM  :  PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_NO_PRIM      Number of clocks where the position request machine has a valid sideband representing a valid subgroup, but is being prevented from making a read request from the position buffer because it has not yet received a valid prim dword from the reuse logic; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the position path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY counts  " = 0xec, 
                            "PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_UTCL1  :  PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_UTCL1      Number of clocks where the position request machine is making a request to the UTCL1 driver logic but the request is not being accepted; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the position path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY and PERF_UTC_POSITION counts  " = 0xed, 
                            "PERF_POS_REQ_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_WRITE  :  PERF_POS_REQ_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_WRITE      Number of times beteen the time the position request machines receives a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP event from sideband memory when the machine is writing one primitive to the prim side of the legacy PA logic; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the position path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_POS_REQ_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_NO_WRITE, the sum of which is the total clocks between the first write after the PERFCOUNTER_START event and the PERFCOUNTER_STOP event.  It can be used with PERF_POS_REQ_QUALIFIED_BUSY  " = 0xee, 
                            "PERF_POS_REQ_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_NO_WRITE  :  PERF_POS_REQ_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_NO_WRITE      Number of clocks beteen the time the position request machines receives a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP event from sideband memory when the machine is not writing anything to the prim side of the legacy PA logic.  The count starts once the first prim is written following the PERFCOUNTER_START event; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the position path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_POS_REQ_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_WRITE, the sum of which is the total clocks between the first write after the PERFCOUNTER_START event and the PERFCOUNTER_STOP event  " = 0xef, 
                            "PERF_POS_REQ_QUALIFIED_BUSY  :  PERF_POS_REQ_QUALIFIED_BUSY     Number of times beteen the time the position request machines reads a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP event from sideband memory when the machine reads a control sideband from sideband memory; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the position path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_POS_REQ_QUALIFIED_STARVED, the sum of which is the total clocks between the first sideband memory read after the PERFCOUNTER_START event and the PERFCOUNTER_STOP event.  It can be used with PERF_POS_REQ_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_WRITE  " = 0xf0, 
                            "PERF_POS_REQ_QUALIFIED_STARVED  :  PERF_POS_REQ_QUALIFIED_STARVED     Number of clocks beteen the time the position request machines reads a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP event from sideband memory when the machine is not reading from sideband memory.  Counting starts after the first sideband memory read following the PERFCOUNTER_START event; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the position path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_POS_REQ_QUALIFIED_BUSY, the sum of which is the total clocks between the first sideband memory read after the PERFCOUNTER_START event and the PERFCOUNTER_STOP event.  It can be used with PERF_POS_REQ_FETCH_TO_PRIMIC_P_FIFO_WRITE  " = 0xf1, 
                            "PERF_POS_RET_FULL_FETCH_TO_SXIF_FIFO  :  PERF_POS_RET_FULL_FETCH_TO_SXIF_FIFO      Number of times where the position receive machine has position data available but is being stalled by a full fetch_to_sxif_fifo; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the position receive path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_POS_RET_FULL_PA_TO_WD_DEALLOC_POSITION_FIFO  " = 0xf2, 
                            "PERF_POS_RET_FULL_PA_TO_WD_DEALLOC_POSITION_FIFO  :  PERF_POS_RET_FULL_PA_TO_WD_DEALLOC_POSITION_FIFO      Number of clocks where the position receive machine has position data available but is being stalled by a full pa_to_wd_dealloc_position_fifo; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the position receive path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_POS_RET_FULL_FETCH_TO_SXIF_FIFO  " = 0xf3, 
                            "PERF_POS_RET_WAITING_ON_RETURNED_CACHELINE  :  PERF_POS_RET_WAITING_ON_RETURNED_CACHELINE      Number of clocks where the position receive machine has been told that it will be receiving a cacheline, and is waiting for the cacheline to be returned; and is waiting for the cacheline to be returned; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks and performance in the position path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_INDEX counts  " = 0xf4, 
                            "PERF_POS_RET_FETCH_TO_SXIF_FIFO_WRITE  :  PERF_POS_RET_FETCH_TO_SXIF_FIFO_WRITE     Number of times the return side of the position machine is writing a position to the SX interface logic in the legacy part of the PA; range-1/clk; it can be used to monitor the position output activity of the NGG logic;  all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_POS_RET_QUALIFIED_BUSY  " = 0xf5, 
                            "PERF_POS_RET_QUALIFIED_BUSY  :  PERF_POS_RET_QUALIFIED_BUSY     Number of times between the position request machne reading a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP events where the return side of the position machine is writing a position to the SX interface logic in the legacy part of the PA; range-1/clk; it can be used as an aide in measuring performance of the NGG logic;  all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_POS_RET_QUALIFIED_STARVED  " = 0xf6, 
                            "PERF_POS_RET_QUALIFIED_STARVED  :  PERF_POS_RET_QUALIFIED_STARVED     Number of clocks between the position request machne reading a PERFCOUNTER_START and PERFCOUNTER_STOP events where the return side of the position machine does NOT write a position to the SX interface logic in the legacy part of the PA; range-1/clk; it can be used as an aide in measuring performance of the NGG logic.  Counting starts on the first write to the SX interface logic after the PERFCOUNTER_START event;  all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_POS_RET_QUALIFIED_STARVED  " = 0xf7, 
                            "PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN0  :  PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN0      Number of clocks where the TC read request latency is less than 64, scaled by the TC_LATENCY_TIME_STAMP_RESOLUTION bits of register PA_CL_ENHANCE; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure average TC latencies with the PA; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN counts  " = 0xf8, 
                            "PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN1  :  PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN1      Number of clocks where the TC read request latency is greater than 64 and less than 128, scaled by the TC_LATENCY_TIME_STAMP_RESOLUTION bits of register PA_CL_ENHANCE; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure average TC latencies with the PA; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN counts  " = 0xf9, 
                            "PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN2  :  PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN2      Number of clocks where the TC read request latency is greater than 128 and less than 192, scaled by the TC_LATENCY_TIME_STAMP_RESOLUTION bits of register PA_CL_ENHANCE; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure average TC latencies with the PA; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN counts  " = 0xfa, 
                            "PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN3  :  PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN3      Number of clocks where the TC read request latency is greater than 192 and less than 256, scaled by the TC_LATENCY_TIME_STAMP_RESOLUTION bits of register PA_CL_ENHANCE; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure average TC latencies with the PA; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN counts  " = 0xfb, 
                            "PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN4  :  PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN4      Number of clocks where the TC read request latency is greater than 256 and less than 320, scaled by the TC_LATENCY_TIME_STAMP_RESOLUTION bits of register PA_CL_ENHANCE; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure average TC latencies with the PA; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN counts  " = 0xfc, 
                            "PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN5  :  PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN5      Number of clocks where the TC read request latency is greater than 320 and less than 384, scaled by the TC_LATENCY_TIME_STAMP_RESOLUTION bits of register PA_CL_ENHANCE; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure average TC latencies with the PA; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN counts  " = 0xfd, 
                            "PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN6  :  PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN6      Number of clocks where the TC read request latency is greater than 384 and less than 512, scaled by the TC_LATENCY_TIME_STAMP_RESOLUTION bits of register PA_CL_ENHANCE; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure average TC latencies with the PA; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN counts  " = 0xfe, 
                            "PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN7  :  PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN7      Number of clocks where the TC read request latency is greater than 512, scaled by the TC_LATENCY_TIME_STAMP_RESOLUTION bits of register PA_CL_ENHANCE; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure average TC latencies with the PA; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN counts  " = 0xff, 
                            "PERF_TC_STREAM0_DATA_AVAILABLE  :  PERF_TC_STREAM0_DATA_AVAILABLE      Number of clocks where the TC return logic has at least one control sideband cachline available but the cacheline is not being consumed; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the sideband path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN counts and other PERF_TC_STREAMn_DATA_AVAILABLE counts " = 0x100, 
                            "PERF_TC_STREAM1_DATA_AVAILABLE  :  PERF_TC_STREAM1_DATA_AVAILABLE      Number of clocks where the TC return logic has at least one index cachline available but the cacheline is not being consumed; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the index path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN counts and other PERF_TC_STREAMn_DATA_AVAILABLE counts " = 0x101, 
                            "PERF_TC_STREAM2_DATA_AVAILABLE  :  PERF_TC_STREAM2_DATA_AVAILABLE      Number of clocks where the TC return logic has at least one position cachline available but the cacheline is not being consumed; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks in the position path; all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_TC_LATENCY_BIN counts and other PERF_TC_STREAMn_DATA_AVAILABLE counts " = 0x102, 
                            "PERF_PAWD_DEALLOC_FIFO_IS_FULL  :  PERF_PAWD_DEALLOC_FIFO_IS_FULL      Number of clocks where either the index or position side of the pa_wd_dealloc_fifo is full; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks; all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_PAWD_DEALLOC_WAITING_TO_BE_READ, PERF_POS_REQ_STALLED_BY_FULL_PA_TO_WD_DEALLOC_INDEX_FIFO, and PERF_POS_RET_FULL_PA_TO_WD_DEALLOC_POSITION_FIFO  " = 0x103, 
                            "PERF_PAWD_DEALLOC_WAITING_TO_BE_READ  :  PERF_PAWD_DEALLOC_WAITING_TO_BE_READ      Number of clocks where the pa_wd_dealloc_fifo has data available for read but is not being read; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks; all instances report the same result; can be combined with PERF_PAWD_DEALLOC_FIFO_IS_FULL  " = 0x104, 
                            "PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT_ON_UTCL1  :  PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT_ON_UTCL1      Number of clocks where shootdown has been asserted, and the PA is waiting for UTCL1 traffic to clear; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to shootdown; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT counts  " = 0x105, 
                            "PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT_ON_UTC_SIDEBAND  :  PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT_ON_UTC_SIDEBAND      Number of clocks where shootdown has been asserted, and the PA is waiting for sideband traffic to clear; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to shootdown; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT counts  " = 0x106, 
                            "PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT_ON_UTC_INDEX  :  PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT_ON_UTC_INDEX      Number of clocks where shootdown has been asserted, and the PA is waiting for index traffic to clear; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to shootdown; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT counts  " = 0x107, 
                            "PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT_ON_UTC_POSITION  :  PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT_ON_UTC_POSITION      Number of clocks where shootdown has been asserted, and the PA is waiting for position traffic to clear; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to shootdown; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT counts  " = 0x108, 
                            "PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT_ALL_CLEAN  :  PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT_ALL_CLEAN      Number of clocks where shootdown has been asserted, and the PA is waiting for all traffic to clear; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to shootdown; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT counts  " = 0x109, 
                            "PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT_DEASSERT  :  PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT_DEASSERT      Number of clocks where shootdown has been asserted and clean has been asserted, and shootdown has not yet been deasserted; range-1/clk; it can be used to measure bottlenecks related to shootdown; all instances report the same result; can be combined with the other PERF_SHOOTDOWN_WAIT counts  " = 0x10a, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_TRANSLATION_MISS_CLIENT0  :  PERF_UTCL1_TRANSLATION_MISS_CLIENT0      Number of clocks UTCL1 Translation miss for sideband client; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x10b, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_TRANSLATION_MISS_CLIENT1  :  PERF_UTCL1_TRANSLATION_MISS_CLIENT1      Number of clocks UTCL1 Translation miss for index client; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x10c, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_TRANSLATION_MISS_CLIENT2  :  PERF_UTCL1_TRANSLATION_MISS_CLIENT2      Number of clocks UTCL1 Translation miss for position client; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x10d, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_PERMISSION_MISS_CLIENT0  :  PERF_UTCL1_PERMISSION_MISS_CLIENT0      Number of clocks UTCL1 Permission miss for sideband client; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x10e, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_PERMISSION_MISS_CLIENT1  :  PERF_UTCL1_PERMISSION_MISS_CLIENT1      Number of clocks UTCL1 Permission miss for index client; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x10f, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_PERMISSION_MISS_CLIENT2  :  PERF_UTCL1_PERMISSION_MISS_CLIENT2      Number of clocks UTCL1 Permission miss for position client; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x110, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_TRANSLATION_HIT_CLIENT0  :  PERF_UTCL1_TRANSLATION_HIT_CLIENT0      Number of clocks UTCL1 Translation hit for sideband client; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x111, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_TRANSLATION_HIT_CLIENT1  :  PERF_UTCL1_TRANSLATION_HIT_CLIENT1      Number of clocks UTCL1 Translation hit for index client; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x112, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_TRANSLATION_HIT_CLIENT2  :  PERF_UTCL1_TRANSLATION_HIT_CLIENT2      Number of clocks UTCL1 Translation hit for position client; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x113, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_REQUEST_CLIENT0  :  PERF_UTCL1_REQUEST_CLIENT0      Number of clocks UTCL1 Request for sideband client; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x114, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_REQUEST_CLIENT1  :  PERF_UTCL1_REQUEST_CLIENT1      Number of clocks UTCL1 Request for index client; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x115, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_REQUEST_CLIENT2  :  PERF_UTCL1_REQUEST_CLIENT2      Number of clocks UTCL1 Request for position client; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x116, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_STALL_MISSFIFO_FULL  :  PERF_UTCL1_STALL_MISSFIFO_FULL      Number of clocks UTCL1 stall missfifo full; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x117, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_STALL_INFLIGHT_MAX  :  PERF_UTCL1_STALL_INFLIGHT_MAX      Number of clocks UTCL1 stall inflight max; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x118, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_STALL_LRU_INFLIGHT  :  PERF_UTCL1_STALL_LRU_INFLIGHT      Number of clocks UTCL1 stall lru inflight; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x119, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_STALL_MULTI_MISS  :  PERF_UTCL1_STALL_MULTI_MISS      Number of clocks UTCL1 stall multi pass; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x11a, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_LFIFO_FULL  :  PERF_UTCL1_LFIFO_FULL      Number of clocks UTCL1 lfifo full; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x11b, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_STALL_LFIFO_NOT_RES_CLIENT0  :  PERF_UTCL1_STALL_LFIFO_NOT_RES_CLIENT0      Number of clocks UTCL1 lfifo not res for sideband client; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x11c, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_STALL_LFIFO_NOT_RES_CLIENT1  :  PERF_UTCL1_STALL_LFIFO_NOT_RES_CLIENT1      Number of clocks UTCL1 lfifo not res for index client; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysifor UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x11d, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_STALL_LFIFO_NOT_RES_CLIENT2  :  PERF_UTCL1_STALL_LFIFO_NOT_RES_CLIENT2      Number of clocks UTCL1 lfifo not res for position client; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x11e, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_STALL_UTCL2_REQ_OUT_OF_CREDITS  :  PERF_UTCL1_STALL_UTCL2_REQ_OUT_OF_CREDITS      Number of clocks UTCL1 stall UTCL2 req out of credits; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x11f, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_UTCL2_REQ  :  PERF_UTCL1_UTCL2_REQ      Number of clocks UTCL1 UTCL2 req; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x120, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_UTCL2_RET  :  PERF_UTCL1_UTCL2_RET      Number of clocks UTCL1 UTCL2 ret; range-1/clk; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x121, 
                            "PERF_UTCL1_UTCL2_INFLIGHT  :  PERF_UTCL1_UTCL2_INFLIGHT      Number of utcl1-utcl2 inflight requests; range-0 to 511; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x122, 
                            "PERF_CLIENT_UTCL1_INFLIGHT  :  PERF_CLIENT_UTCL1_INFLIGHT      Number of client-utcl1 inflight requests; range-0 to 511; it can be used for UTCL1 performance analysis; all instances report the same result; can be combined with other PERF_UTCL1 counts  " = 0x123 }  ;
    CNTR_MODE  23:20  ALPHA {"PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_ACCUM  :  Accumulate increment values over enabled cycles. " = 0x0, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_ACTIVE_CYCLES  :  Count the number of cycles with a nonzero increment value. " = 0x1, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_MAX  :  Store the largest increment value received over cycles counted. " = 0x2, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_DIRTY  :  Record whether a nonzero increment value was ever received. " = 0x3, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_SAMPLE  :  Just record the latest increment vlaue. " = 0x4, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_CYCLES_SINCE_FIRST_EVENT  :  Count the cycles since a nonzero increment value. " = 0x5, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_CYCLES_SINCE_LAST_EVENT  :  Count the cycles since a zero increment value. " = 0x6, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_CYCLES_GE_HI  :  Count the cycles with an increment greater than or equal to the value in the high bits. " = 0x7, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_CYCLES_EQ_HI  :  Count the cycles with an increment equal to the value in the high bits. " = 0x8, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_INACTIVE_CYCLES  :  Count the number of cycles with a zero increment value. " = 0x9, 
                            "PERFMON_COUNTER_MODE_RESERVED  :  This is here just so this is a 4 bit field in case we add modes in the future.  Don't use it. " = 0xf }  ;
};

PA_SU_PERFCOUNTER1_SELECT1   <GpuF0Reg:0x3640c> <GpuF1Reg:0x3640c>   32    {
    PERF_SEL2  9:0  ALPHA {"PERF_PAPC_PASX_REQ  :  PERF_PAPC_PASX_REQ                     Number of PA->SX requests; increment rate-one per clock (each req leads to 4 cycles of data from SX); range-1/clk, it does not indicate bad performance; it cannot be used to locate bottlenecks; all instances report the same result; can be combined with PASX_FIRST_VECTOR,PASX_SECOND_VECTOR, PASX_VTX_KILL_DISCARD, PASX_VTX_NAN_DISCARD, PASX_FIRST_DEAD, PASX_FIRST_DEAD  " = 0x0, 
                            "PERF_PAPC_PASX_DISABLE_PIPE  :  PERF_PAPC_PASX_DISABLE_PIPE            Number of transfers lost due to disabled pipe; increment rate-one per clock ; range-1/clk ; does not indicate bad performance; cannot be used for bottleneck location; all instances report the same result; no combinations " = 0x1, 
                            "PERF_PAPC_PASX_FIRST_VECTOR  :  PERF_PAPC_PASX_FIRST_VECTOR            Number of First Vectors from SX to PA;  increment rate-one per clock ;  range-1/clk ; it does not indicate bad performance; no bottleneck detection;all instances report the same result; no combinations " = 0x2, 
                            "PERF_PAPC_PASX_SECOND_VECTOR  :  PERF_PAPC_PASX_SECOND_VECTOR           Number of Second Vectors from SX to PA; increment rate-one per clock ;  range-1/clk ; it does not indicate bad performance; no bottleneck detection;all instances report the same result; no combinations " = 0x3, 
                            "PERF_PAPC_PASX_FIRST_DEAD  :  PERF_PAPC_PASX_FIRST_DEAD              Number of Unused First Vectors (due to granularity of 4); increment rate-one per clock ;  range-1/clk;it does not indicate bad performance; no bottleneck detection;all instances report the same result; no combinations " = 0x4, 
                            "PERF_PAPC_PASX_SECOND_DEAD  :  PERF_PAPC_PASX_SECOND_DEAD             Number of Unused Second Vectors (due to granularity of 4); increment rate-one per clock ;  range-1/clk;it does not indicate bad performance; no bottleneck detection;all instances report the same result; no combinations " = 0x5, 
